86 /* Discussions
87 1. Dafny is super bad at slicing (esp. nested slicing).
88   Do circumvent it whenever possible. It can save you a lot of assertions & lemmas!
89 
90   For example, instead of `palindromic(s[i..j])`, use the pattern `palindromic(s, i, j)` instead.
91   I didn't realize this (ref: https://github.com/Nangos/dafleet/commit/3302ddd7642240ff2b2f6a8c51e8becd5c9b6437),
92   Resulting in a couple of clumsy lemmas.
93 
94 2. Bonus -- Manacher's algorithm
95   Our above solution needs `O(|s|^2)` time in the worst case. Can we improve it? Yes.
96 
97   Manacher's algorithm guarantees an `O(|s|)` time.
98   To get the intuition, ask yourself: when will it really take `O(|s|^2)` time?
99   When there are a lot of "nesting and overlapping" palindromes. like in `abcbcbcba` or even `aaaaaa`.
100 
101   Imagine each palindrome as a "mirror". "Large mirrors" reflect "small mirrors".
102   Therefore, when we "expand" from some "center", we can "reuse" some information from its "mirrored center".
103   For example, we move the "center", from left to right, in the string `aiaOaia...`
104   Here, the char `O` is the "large mirror".
105   When the current center is the second `i`, it is "mirrored" to the first `i` (which we've calculated for),
106   so we know the palindrome centered at the second `i` must have at least a length of 3 (`aia`).
107   So we can expand directly from `aia`, instead of expanding from scratch.
108 
109   Manacher's algorithm is verified below.
110   Also, I will verify that "every loop is entered for only `O(|s|)` times",
111   which "indirectly" proves that the entire algorithm runs in `O(|s|)` time.
112 */
113 
